  "rationale": "With no defences, the shortest attack takes 10 techniques. Every exfiltration step needs admin on the db, fileserver or backup host. Getting there needs stolen_dbadmin, which comes only from admin_dc or admin_adfs. Those need stolen_admin, which comes only from kerberoasting. Kerberoasting needs a foothold on the appserver or apiserver, which needs reach_internal and stolen_user. Shortest chain: (1) phish_workstation gives foothold_workstation and stolen_user; (2) pivot_internal gives reach_internal, since the network is not segmented; (3) auth_appserver gives foothold_appserver; (4) kerberoast_dc gives stolen_admin; (5) auth_dc gives foothold_dc; (6) escalate_dc gives admin_dc; (7) dump_dbadmin_dc gives stolen_dbadmin; (8) auth_db gives foothold_db; (9) escalate_db gives admin_db; (10) exfiltrate_db gives exfiltrated. Each prerequisite in this chain can be produced only by techniques of equal or greater cost, so no shorter path exists. The ADFS route has the same length."
